course: dictionary
lesson: 1772
title: Cleverly: smart or sly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cleverly is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something, and it usually means in a smart way, using good thinking or skill. «Toad cleverly invites them to lunch» tells you Toad has a plan, not that he is just being nice.
explain: Cleverly can also mean in a tricky or cunning way, to fool someone. The fox cleverly tricks the crow. Read the clues around the word: if someone is being fooled, or someone is getting something they should not have, the tricky meaning is the right one.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A camel's hump stores fat, not water; camels save water very cleverly» works with the smart meaning, because camels use water well. Ask yourself: is this person being clever, or are they tricking someone?
explain: You will often see cleverly in phrases such as cleverly designed, cleverly hidden and cleverly worked out. A cleverly designed box uses its space well, and a cleverly worked out maths problem uses a short trick. Notice the word after cleverly, because it gives you another clue.
fact: Cleverly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: Cleverly means in a smart, clever way, using good thinking or skill.
fact: Cleverly can also mean in a tricky or cunning way, to fool someone.
fact: The tricky meaning shows up when someone is being fooled, as when «the fox cleverly tricks the crow».
fact: Phrases such as cleverly designed, cleverly hidden and cleverly worked out are common in stories, maths and design.
exercise: In «Toad cleverly invites them to lunch», what does cleverly mean? | Slowly and sadly | Loudly and rudely | *In a smart, clever way | In a hurry
exercise: A camel «can drink a huge amount at once» because it saves water «very cleverly». What does saving water very cleverly mean? | *Using it well, with good thinking | Hiding it in a box | Pouring it away | Wasting it on purpose
exercise: Which phrase describes a plan that is smart and well thought out? | cleverly sneezed | *cleverly worked out | cleverly lost | cleverly shouted
test: In «the fox cleverly tricks the crow», what does cleverly mean? | Forgets the crow | *In a cunning way, to fool someone | Sings loudly | Helps the crow
test: «When she notices the Queen listening behind her, she cleverly changes» the words. What does cleverly show about how she changes them? | By mistake | Loudly, so the Queen can hear | Carelessly, without any thought | *With a smart, quick trick
exam: Which sentence uses cleverly in the tricky, fool-someone sense? | The camel cleverly saves water | Toad cleverly invites them to lunch | The box is cleverly designed | *The fox cleverly tricks the crow
